        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A 3500 watt generator is a 120 volt essentials machine with a working budget of about 2,800 watts. It keeps the refrigerator and freezer cold, the furnace blower and lights on, and a 30-amp RV comfortable, including the rooftop air conditioner if you fit a soft starter and keep the microwave off while it runs. It trips from habits, mostly stacked heating appliances and simultaneous motor starts, more often than from being undersized.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If your list includes a well pump, a big sump pump, anything on 240V, or two comfort loads at once, it is the wrong size and the 5,000 watt class is the next step. If it fits your list, our <a href="/best-3500-watt-generator/" class="text-[#38BDF8] font-semibold hover:underline">3500 watt generator picks</a> compare the current models on the numbers that matter.
